{:edb/db-before-t 2086 :edb/db-after-t 2087 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535399 50 #inst "2026-10-08T23:19:08.214Z" 13194139535399 true] [17592186087703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347200 13194139535399 true] [17592186087737 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347193 13194139535399 true] [17592186087738 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347207 13194139535399 true] [17592186087738 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347212 13194139535399 true] [17592186347193 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347194 13194139535399 true] [17592186347193 1089 "q-121908" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347193 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535399 true] [17592186347193 1100 "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨3t-1,\\sqrt{2t+1}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=4.$" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347193 1113 #uuid "f86f6880-2810-590a-a6b3-f2816b5d8154" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347193 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2t+1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2t+1}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=4,$ we substitute $t=4$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(4) & =⟨3,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2(4)+1}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347194 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347195 13194139535399 true] [17592186347194 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347196 13194139535399 true] [17592186347194 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347197 13194139535399 true] [17592186347194 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347198 13194139535399 true] [17592186347194 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347199 13194139535399 true] [17592186347194 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535399 true] [17592186347194 1041 "selection" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347194 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347197 13194139535399 true] [17592186347194 1110 #uuid "2e18736b-841d-5062-bb69-3c86541b8c93" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347195 1034 "a(4)=⟨4,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347195 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535399 true] [17592186347195 1111 #uuid "c36679ec-d687-5e56-b976-cfac53665ba6" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347196 1034 "a(4)=⟨3,\\sqrt{3}⟩" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347196 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535399 true] [17592186347196 1111 #uuid "9dad882a-a310-5568-84a7-f53fd42e33f2" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347197 1034 "a(4)=⟨3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347197 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535399 true] [17592186347197 1111 #uuid "1d3a132f-25a5-5bf7-afa1-8da607228a17" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347198 1034 "a(4)=⟨4,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟩" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347198 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535399 true] [17592186347198 1111 #uuid "21fd382a-22ba-5c24-9097-373376910b53" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347199 1034 "a(4)=⟨11,\\sqrt{3}⟩" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347199 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535399 true] [17592186347199 1111 #uuid "e72f3e49-2d09-5108-91cb-8ef8d18440f4" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347200 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347201 13194139535399 true] [17592186347200 1089 "q-121931" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347200 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535399 true] [17592186347200 1100 "The position vector $r(t)$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨4t-{t}^{3},2{t}^{2}+t⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a.$" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347200 1113 #uuid "13d7a5d0-065f-59fe-97e0-96a304f6f591" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347200 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-{t}^{3}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}+t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4-3{t}^{2},4t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4-3{t}^{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6t,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347201 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347202 13194139535399 true] [17592186347201 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347203 13194139535399 true] [17592186347201 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347204 13194139535399 true] [17592186347201 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347205 13194139535399 true] [17592186347201 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347206 13194139535399 true] [17592186347201 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535399 true] [17592186347201 1041 "selection" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347201 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347206 13194139535399 true] [17592186347201 1110 #uuid "0b4a9a5f-e003-510d-b35e-8c68d5714506" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347202 1034 "a=⟨-3{t}^{2},4⟩" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347202 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535399 true] [17592186347202 1111 #uuid "4227cabc-59d9-5286-984b-9cd00248c30b" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347203 1034 "a=⟨-3{t}^{2},2⟩" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347203 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535399 true] [17592186347203 1111 #uuid "45880911-8170-51f3-8d9d-11976c063c97" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347204 1034 "a=⟨-6t,4t+1⟩" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347204 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535399 true] [17592186347204 1111 #uuid "06070c3c-03c8-5eb6-bc5e-5ed35e412ad5" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347205 1034 "a=⟨-4t,4t+1⟩" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347205 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535399 true] [17592186347205 1111 #uuid "9bb8d6c8-3f2f-5717-a97d-f2279c934094" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347206 1034 "a=⟨-6t,4⟩" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347206 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535399 true] [17592186347206 1111 #uuid "6cf75821-19b0-5f6b-a3e4-36505e10fa5b" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347207 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347208 13194139535399 true] [17592186347207 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347210 13194139535399 true] [17592186347207 1089 "q-347197" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347207 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535399 true] [17592186347207 1100 "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+1,\\,4+{t}^{2}-{t}^{3}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=0.$ Do not round the answers.\n\n$a(0)=⟨${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$⟩$" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347207 1113 #uuid "7d8918a7-328e-53cc-86ce-67ceda4d8417" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347207 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4+{t}^{2}-{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-4t,\\,2t-3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-4t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6t-4,\\,2-6t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=0,$ we substitute $t=0$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =⟨6(0)-4,\\,2-6(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347208 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347209 13194139535399 true] [17592186347208 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535399 true] [17592186347208 1041 "field-1" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347208 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347209 13194139535399 true] [17592186347208 1110 #uuid "9e492577-8f3c-597b-ba0c-62eec5ca3e38" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347209 1034 "-4" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347209 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535399 true] [17592186347209 1111 #uuid "9de2f21c-6e35-5193-a53d-3a790e6bde9b" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347210 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347211 13194139535399 true] [17592186347210 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535399 true] [17592186347210 1041 "field-2" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347210 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347211 13194139535399 true] [17592186347210 1110 #uuid "1808fa0e-76a3-57c7-ba26-612284b512c3" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347211 1034 "2" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347211 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535399 true] [17592186347211 1111 #uuid "30cfb7b2-1ef0-559b-9da5-320d1575e984" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347212 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347213 13194139535399 true] [17592186347212 1089 "q-85609" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347212 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535399 true] [17592186347212 1100 "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨{e}^{2-t},\\,3+{t}^{4}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=2.$" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347212 1113 #uuid "7c35299e-e7ea-52d7-8411-4ed07a1c0894" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347212 1145 "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3+{t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{2-t},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{e}^{2-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{2-t},\\,12{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(2) & =⟨{e}^{2-2},12(2)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,48⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347213 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347214 13194139535399 true] [17592186347213 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347215 13194139535399 true] [17592186347213 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347216 13194139535399 true] [17592186347213 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347217 13194139535399 true] [17592186347213 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347218 13194139535399 true] [17592186347213 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535399 true] [17592186347213 1041 "selection" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347213 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347218 13194139535399 true] [17592186347213 1110 #uuid "7f22f698-3cf0-5dd8-a9d7-98c5b05260ef" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347214 1034 "a(2)=⟨-1,24⟩" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347214 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535399 true] [17592186347214 1111 #uuid "63d4599a-28d2-53e3-b499-79234ac86f20" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347215 1034 "a(2)=⟨0,48⟩" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347215 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535399 true] [17592186347215 1111 #uuid "5bc8ef76-2f41-5d8d-a2d6-3d805f6e3172" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347216 1034 "a(2)=⟨1,96⟩" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347216 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535399 true] [17592186347216 1111 #uuid "585c8299-7145-545e-84c1-d5bdccfef4d2" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347217 1034 "a(2)=⟨0,24⟩" 13194139535399 true] [17592186347217 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535399 true] [17592186347217 1111 #uuid "70e28c51-ce40-5e60-860e-c88